SPM PCM code for the MT6735M (Meizu M5c), for the forge 4.9 kernel (m5c-4.9-a13).

Not proprietary blobs: generated from the GPL C arrays of the m5c 3.18 kernel
(commit 55c14fdc; drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/spm_v1/
mt_spm_{sleep,sodi,dpidle}.c, block CONFIG_ARCH_MT6735M, and
mt6735/mt_spm_vcore_dvfs_2.c) by a small converter script (pcm2bin.py, not part
of this tree).

Why: the 4.9 kernel loads the MT6735M SPM code only from these four files
(request_firmware on open of /dev/spm, spm_v1/mt_spm.c:82-119, 618-697) and
refuses to suspend until all four are loaded ("SPM FIRMWARE IS NOT READY",
mt6735/mt_sleep.c:275).  Stock Flyme 6.0.2.4G keeps the same code inside its
3.18 kernel and ships no pcm files.  File format: mt_spm.c:660-685.

Match with the 4.9 driver (checked 2026-09-29): pcm_vcore_dvfs_2.bin is word
for word the array 4.9 still embeds (mt6735/mt_spm_vcore_dvfs_2.c,
v0.5.8_20150904); the pwr_ctrl tables and SPM flags that drive the suspend,
SODI and deep-idle code are identical between the 3.18 and 4.9 sources; 4.9
uses the version string only for logging.  The stock kernel carries newer
suspend/sodi/deepidle builds (v..._20160311) - the fallback if these
misbehave.

The .bin files are tracked (added with -f past vendor/.gitignore's *.bin,
2026-09-29): a clean checkout must not build a vendor image without them.
To recreate them, run pcm2bin.py over drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power of that
kernel tree with vendor/meizu/m5c/firmware/spm as the output directory and
compare with SHA256SUMS.
